/*
 * Copyright 2026 NXP
 * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 *
 * System-PM constraint layer: mark which SoC power states the VREF block does not
 * survive. Stacked on top of the per-board overlay in boards/ for the system
 * phase (via EXTRA_DTC_OVERLAY_FILE, so the board overlay is still picked up
 * automatically).
 *
 * Only &deeppowerdown is listed. The reference is in the CORE domain: Deep Sleep
 * and Power Down leave its registers and its bandgap alone -- which is the point
 * of a reference that a converter can keep using in a low-power state -- while
 * Deep Power Down resets the block, and it is the one state the SoC dtsi already
 * names in core_domain's onoff-power-states. So this file restates a claim the
 * devicetree already makes rather than adding a new one.
 *
 * Nothing is expected to act on it: the driver takes no policy lock, because an
 * enabled reference is not an operation in flight. The declaration is what an
 * application would read to decide whether it has to re-enable the output after
 * a transition, and the phase checks the other half -- that no lock is held on
 * the reference's behalf.
 */

&vref {
	zephyr,disabling-power-states = <&deeppowerdown>;
};
